---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {modTools} from '../../data/mod-tools';
import snapshot from '../../data/releases.json';
export function getStaticPaths(){return modTools.map(tool=>({params:{slug:tool.slug},props:{tool}}));}
const {tool}=Astro.props;
const release=snapshot.gameReleases[tool.slug as keyof typeof snapshot.gameReleases];
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title={tool.title+' — TigerFury Fixes'} description={tool.description}><div class="shell detail"><a class="text-link" href={base+'mod-tools/'}>← All mod tools</a><p class="eyebrow mt-10">MOD TOOLS · WINDOWS X64</p><h1>{tool.title}</h1><p class="lead">Extract. Edit. Repack.</p><p class="reading-width">{tool.description} The C# Windows Forms app is built for the inspected little-endian XFIR/FGDC compressed cast format in CSI: Dark Motives.</p><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6"><a class="button primary" href="#downloads">Download the tool ↓</a><a class="button secondary" href={tool.source+'#readme'}>Documentation ↗</a></div><img class="tool-screenshot" src={base+tool.image} alt="CSI Cast Tool Windows interface with Extract cast and Repack project controls" width="856" height="629"/><section class="detail-section reading-width"><h2>Inside the tool</h2><ul class="tool-features"><li>Export raw resources and complete JPEG-backed images as editable PNGs.</li><li>Generate contact sheets to find scenes visually.</li><li>Detect edited PNGs and embed replacements when repacking.</li><li>Fit edited images to the original dimensions by default.</li><li>Preserve unchanged resource payloads and verify the rebuilt payload set.</li><li>Open extraction projects made by the earlier Python tool.</li></ul></section><section id="downloads" class="detail-section"><h2>Downloads</h2><p>Self-contained Windows x64 release. No Python, Director or separately installed .NET runtime is required.</p><p class="section-note">Release {release.tag} · Published <time datetime={release.publishedAt}>{new Date(release.publishedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{day:'numeric',month:'short',year:'numeric',timeZone:'UTC'})}</time> · Checked {snapshot.checkedAt}</p><ul class="download-choices">{release.assets.map(asset=><li><div><h3>CSI Cast Tool for Windows</h3><p>Extract the ZIP and run CSI-Cast-Tool.exe.</p><small>{asset.name}</small></div><a class="button primary" href={asset.url}>Download ZIP ↓</a></li>)}</ul><a class="text-link" href={release.url}>Release notes ↗</a></section><section class="detail-section reading-width"><h2>How to use it</h2><ol class="tool-features"><li>Choose Extract cast, select your .cct and create a new extraction project.</li><li>Use the contact sheets to find an image. Edit its PNG in the Images folder, keeping the filename.</li><li>Keep Fit edited PNGs to original dimensions checked, then repack project.json to a new .cct filename.</li><li>Close the game, back up the installed cast outside the game folder, and manually install the rebuilt cast in its original location.</li><li>Test the scene, transitions, tools and hotspots. Restore your backup if needed.</li></ol></section><section class="detail-section reading-width"><h2>Editing limits</h2><p>This is an experimental cast editor for the inspected Dark Motives format. Only complete JPEG resources are decoded to PNG; scripts, sound, BITD and other resources remain raw. It does not recover editable Director source.</p><p>Full-resolution replacements do not update scene geometry or scripts. Fit mode preserves the original pixel dimensions; use matching proportions to avoid stretching. Transparent PNG replacements are unsupported.</p><p>The repository reports synthetic checks and an unchanged round trip of the inspected Case 2 cast. Replacements built by this C# version still need in-game testing.</p></section><section class="game-support"><div><h2>Project links</h2><p>Read the complete format limits and installation instructions before editing your game.</p><a class="text-link" href={base+'fixes/csi-dark-motives/'}>CSI: Dark Motives compatibility fix →</a></div><a class="button secondary" href={tool.source+'/issues'}>Report an issue ↗</a></section></div></Layout>
